From: FAROVITUS <farovitus@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:08:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: re-read the battery percent setting only when
 charging changes

BatteryMeterView.onBatteryLevelChanged() called updateShowPercent() on
every battery broadcast while a cable was in. updateShowPercent() reads
STATUS_BAR_SHOW_BATTERY_PERCENT through LineageSettings, a binder call to
the settings provider, although that setting has its own content observer
in BatteryMeterViewController. Only the charging state feeds the result
from here, and the call was skipped exactly when charging stopped.

On my phone (Exynos 7420, SystemUI on the A53 cores) a simpleperf
profile of 8 battery broadcasts put 12 % of SystemUI's main-thread CPU
time (about 6 ms per broadcast) in this read. BatteryService sends a broadcast for every new
voltage while charging, so this ran several times a minute.

Re-read the setting when charging starts or stops, which also fixes the
missed update on unplug. Not built or tested yet.

Signed-off-by: FAROVITUS <farovitus@gmail.com>
---
 .../src/com/android/systemui/battery/BatteryMeterView.java  | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/battery/BatteryMeterView.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/battery/BatteryMeterView.java
index 2b858f5..705b391 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/battery/BatteryMeterView.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/battery/BatteryMeterView.java
@@ -260,7 +260,11 @@ public class BatteryMeterView extends LinearLayout implements DarkReceiver {
         mAccessorizedDrawable.setBatteryLevel(level);
         mCircleDrawable.setBatteryLevel(level);
         updatePercentText();
-        if (pluggedIn) {
+        // Whether the percent shows depends on the charging state; the Lineage
+        // setting itself has its own observer. Re-read it only when charging
+        // starts or stops, not on every battery broadcast while plugged in:
+        // each read is a binder call to the LineageSettings provider.
+        if (isCharging != wasCharging) {
             updateShowPercent();
         }
 
